      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "\"Taking the pressure off\" means letting go of the exhausting obligation to *fix* or *understand* the massive, unsolvable problems. You don't have to be a savior or a hopeful participant in a doomed play. You can simply choose to be the one who steps off the stage, finding a quiet, immediate peace in the act of simply *not* trying to carry all that weight anymore. It's not giving up; it's choosing a more manageable reality.",
